**How to implement.** An excluded point stays in the data and leaves what is validated, and the badge says how many are excluded (001 §K 'Raw data is immutable; exclusions carry a reason …'; 001 §K 'Status badges: no data / mapped / validated (points) / excluded points / data changed / out of range'; the S9.1 mapper's request: the excluded-points badge joins `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck`). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ImportProfiles.fs`, after `selectedBy` (step 305): `type MappedPoints with member this.keptBy (exclusions : PointExclusion list) : MappedPoints`, the points in order without those whose `MappedPointNumber` (step 313) an exclusion names, the case kept: `SeriesPoints` keeps its series' kind (`IntensityData` or `EllipsometricData`, `MeasuredData.fs:MeasuredSeries`) over the kept points, and each list case its kept items; an exclusion naming no point changes nothing. It is the one rule from an attachment's exclusions to the points a validation reads, and the one a study's residual reads in S11. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: `loadAndValidate` (steps 291, 304, 305) is `dataProxy.readMapped data`, then `keptBy data.exclusions`, then `validatedFor` as before, so an excluded point is never out of range and never counted as validated. `ExperimentDataBadge` (step 295) gains `ExcludedPointsBadge of kept : MeasuredPointCount * excluded : MeasuredPointCount` after `ValidatedDataBadge`, its `text` `excluded points (<k> excluded, <n> validated)`; `ofCheck` answers it, in place of `ValidatedDataBadge`, for an `Ok points` outcome of a mapped attachment whose `exclusions` are not empty, `kept` being the points' `pointCount` and `excluded` the number of exclusions; every other branch, and its order, is unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `ExperimentDataBadge.caption` (step 295) answers `Loaded — <n> point(s) kept, <k> excluded` for it, every other caption unchanged. The two callers of `loadAndValidate` are authorized and nothing in them changes: `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, whose `model.dataBadgeOf` and one private validation function (steps 295, 304) already pass the experiment's mapped attachment to `ofCheck`, and `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment`), which counts the validated points it answers. No other member, case or option is added. Tests. `ImportProfileTests` (step 300) gains `kept points leave out the excluded ones and keep the rest in order`: over a two-point intensity series, three Phone ROI rows and three `Lab scan` rows (step 300's test-local fixtures), excluding point 2 keeps points 1 and 3 of each list in order and the series' first point as an `IntensityData` series; no exclusion keeps each whole; and an exclusion of point 9 changes nothing. `ExperimentDataProxyTests`: `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation` (steps 295, 304) also answers `ExcludedPointsBadge (MeasuredPointCount 2, MeasuredPointCount 1)` for an attachment excluding one point whose outcome is `Ok` of two points, whose `text` is `excluded points (1 excluded, 2 validated)`, and keeps `DataChangedBadge` ahead of it for a changed file; and it gains `loading data validates the kept points, so an excluded point outside the range does not refuse the data`: over its mock (step 305), answering for a test-local attachment the canned three-point intensity series `0 → 1.0`, `45 → 0.5`, `90 → 0.0`, step 288's one-axis experiment over R1 0…45° answers `DataRangeMismatchErr` naming `90` with no exclusion, and `Ok (SeriesPoints _)` of two points when the attachment excludes point 3 (`beam blocked`).

**Acceptance.** After kept points land, `MappedPoints.keptBy` MUST leave out exactly the excluded points, `loadAndValidate` MUST validate only the kept points, and `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck` MUST answer `ExcludedPointsBadge` (kept and excluded counts) for validated data with exclusions, its caption `Loaded — <n> point(s) kept, <k> excluded`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `kept points leave out the excluded ones and keep the rest in order` and `loading data validates the kept points, so an excluded point outside the range does not refuse the data`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `the data badge follows the attachment, its file's hash and its validation`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
